{
  "$doc": [
    "FROZEN — the identity table of the v1 plan set. The ids are never regenerated.",
    "",
    "WHY IT EXISTS. Before this package a predefined plan's id WAS its index in the",
    "asset array (predefined_workout_plan_model.dart:57). That index is PERSISTED: a",
    "guest's chosen plan is stored as selectedWorkoutPlanId in FlutterSecureStorage",
    "(Keychain / EncryptedSharedPreferences, so it survives app updates and, on iOS,",
    "reinstalls) and resolved against a LATER load of the asset when they register.",
    "Reorder the file between those two moments and the guest silently receives a",
    "different plan than the one they previewed.",
    "",
    "WHAT IT STORES. index -> { stable id, name, nameEn }. ONE ROW PER PLAN, NOT PER",
    "FILE: the same plan is written twice, once per language, and index i of",
    "predefined_workout_plans.json and of predefined_workout_plans_en.json is the same",
    "plan (verified at generation: same exercise ids, same duration, same session",
    "count). The table has to carry BOTH names because the reader resolves a document",
    "by the name it reads, and an English document only ever says its English name.",
    "A table with the Spanish column alone made every English plan unresolvable.",
    "",
    "THE NAME IS THE LOAD-BEARING HALF: an id alone cannot find a plan again once the",
    "array moved. The 82 Spanish names are unique. The English ones are NOT — indices",
    "11 and 48 both read \"Volume Push Pull Legs\", which is a copy defect of the v1",
    "asset and not something this table may fix — so a name that matches more than one",
    "row is disambiguated by the index, and a name that matches none rejects the plan",
    "rather than dropping it in silence. Pinned in both directions and for both",
    "languages by legacy_v1_id_map_pin_test.",
    "",
    "DO NOT regenerate against a reordered asset — that reintroduces the very bug.",
    "DO NOT add entries: new content is v2, which carries its own written planId."
  ],
